    - dielectric 'd' on z: 10.0 cells per λ_eff (eps_r=9.00, freq_max=5GHz, dx=2mm). Need ≥15 cells/λ_eff for phase-accurate propagation. Yee without subpixel smoothing has 1st-order convergence at ε interfaces.
    - Material 'd' (geometry entry #0, Box) extends into CPML region along x-axis: bbox lo face at -1m is 1m past the x-lo absorber boundary at 0mm. CPML modifies field updates — geometry inside the absorber is physically meaningless (issue #61).
    - all dielectric(s) ['d'] are perfectly lossless in an open (CPML) domain. If you are measuring Q / resonance, this gives an ARTIFICIALLY infinite Q (design-guide Anti-Pattern #1, an R5 surface-metric trap) — add loss, e.g. sigma = 2*pi*f*eps0*eps_r*tan_delta. (Harmless if you are not measuring Q.)
